// Classify one node of a caller's range (../walk.id) into an edge, or
// nothing: k_of/s1_of (../../../../../../../front/tree/node/) are read here,
// not re-derived -- the same two kinds reach_mark's scan_reach tests for the
// same reason (mid/names/exports/reach/dead/more/scan.id), unconditionally
// rather than gated by reachability, because --calls reports the whole graph
// a build would prune from, not what a build would keep.
scan_call_edge(int id, string caller) {
  string k = k_of(id);
  if(k == "call") {
    call_edge_emit(caller, id, "call");
  }
  if(k == "var") {
    scan_call_value(id, caller);
  }
} return void;
given edge_fixture ((import edge_call_node), "edge_caller"):() then check_failed:(0)
given edge_fixture ((import edge_var_node), "edge_caller"):() then check_failed:(0)

// A name used as a value is an edge only when it names a function
// (call_callee_loc's membership test again, ../line.id) -- reach_add ignores
// a plain variable's name the same way, so a local that happens to share a
// name with nothing in `fnames` is silently not an edge.
//
// KNOWN OVER-REPORT: finish_atom (front/parse/expr/atom/lit/call/call.id)
// builds a "var" node for every bare identifier before it knows whether a
// '(' follows, and when one does, that var node is never removed -- it is
// simply not on the tree a real value-read would leave, but it is still in
// the flat id range this file's caller (../walk.id) scans, the same range
// scan_reach (mid/names/exports/reach/dead/more/scan.id) has always scanned
// for reachability, where one extra name in a set is harmless. So every
// direct call also prints a "value" row for the same callee: a value row
// with no matching call row is a real value use (an export, a parameter, a
// `func(...) return ...`-typed local); one that matches a call row for the
// same caller and callee is this artifact, not a second real use. Fixing it
// at the source means resolving a call before finish_atom decides whether to
// keep the var node it already built, which is a parser change past this
// task's scope; idc/README.md's "The function dependency tree" section says
// so.
scan_call_value(int id, string caller) {
  string name = s1_of(id);
  if(find_str((import fnames), name) >= 0) {
    call_edge_emit(caller, id, "value");
  }
} return void;
